  "hr.exit_interview": [["end", "use", "How this information is used", "What you tell us in this interview is used by HR to understand why people leave and to improve the workplace. It is treated confidentially: HR reports themes to management in summary form and does not identify you without your permission, except where the law or the safety of a person requires it. Taking part is voluntary, and you may decline any question."]],
  "hr.experience": [["end", "terms", "Purpose of this certificate", "This certificate records the period of service and the designation held, on the basis of the Company's records, and is issued to the employee at the employee's request. It is not a character certificate and does not describe the circumstances in which the employment ended. It may be shown to prospective employers and educational institutions."]],
  "hr.fnf": [["end", "notes", "Notes to the statement", "This statement is prepared from the Company's payroll and leave records up to the last working day, and from the clearance given by each department. Amounts are stated before or after the deductions shown, as indicated, and tax is deducted at source as the law requires. Any amount found to be due after this statement because of a later correction will be settled by the Company and the employee on the same basis. The employee should check the figures and raise any query before signing."]],
  "hr.salary_cert": [["end", "scope", "Basis and validity", "This certificate states the compensation of the employee as on the date of issue, from the Company's payroll records, and is issued at the employee's request for the purpose stated above. It does not create any obligation on the Company, and it is valid only for that purpose. The Company may be asked to confirm its authenticity and will do so on written request."]],
  "hr.verification": [["end", "scope", "Basis of this letter", "The details in this letter are confirmed from the Company's records and are given in response to a written request and with the consent of the employee, in line with the Company's confidentiality obligations and with applicable data protection law. The Company does not give any opinion on the employee's performance or conduct in this letter. Please address any further query to the HR department."]],
  "hr.leave_policy": [["end", "responsibilities", "Responsibilities", "Employees are responsible for planning their leave so that work is covered, for applying within the notice stated in this policy and for keeping their own balances in view. Managers are responsible for deciding requests fairly and promptly, for protecting business continuity, and for making sure that employees are able to take the leave they are entitled to. HR is responsible for maintaining accurate leave records, for explaining this policy and for resolving disputes about balances."], ["end", "review", "Review of this policy", "This policy is owned by {{input.policy_owner}} and takes effect from {{input.effective_date|date}}. It is reviewed whenever the law changes and otherwise at regular intervals, and any change is communicated to employees before it applies. Where this policy and a statute differ, the statute prevails. Employees who are unsure how this policy applies to them should ask HR."]],
  "hr.attendance_policy": [["end", "records", "Records and monitoring", "Attendance is recorded through the Company's HR system, and every employee must record their own attendance only; recording attendance for another person is a serious breach of this policy. The Company keeps attendance records for the period the law and its retention policy require, and uses them for payroll, leave and the review of working patterns, in line with its data protection obligations."], ["end", "responsibilities", "Responsibilities and enforcement", "Employees must keep to the working days and hours in this policy and report any absence to their manager at the earliest. Managers must review the attendance of their teams, approve exceptions fairly and refer repeated or unexplained absence to HR. HR maintains this policy and applies it consistently. Failure to follow it may lead to action under the Company's disciplinary procedure, after the employee has been heard."]],
  "hr.wfh_policy": [["end", "conduct", "Working remotely: expectations", "Employees who work remotely must be available during the core hours stated in this policy, respond to colleagues and managers promptly, and keep their calendar and status up to date. They must maintain a working environment in which Company and customer information cannot be seen or overheard by others, and they must follow the Company's information security policy as they would in the office.", "Remote work does not change an employee's terms of employment, entitlement to leave, or obligations on confidentiality and conduct. The Company may ask an employee to attend the office when the needs of the business require it."], ["end", "review", "Review and withdrawal", "This policy is owned by {{input.policy_owner}} and applies from {{input.effective_date|date}}. Remote work is a facility and not a right. The Company may change or withdraw it for an individual or a team, with reasons and reasonable notice, where the work, performance or security needs of the business require."]],
  "hr.grievance": [["end", "principles", "Principles", "Every employee has the right to raise a concern about their work or workplace without fear of retaliation. Grievances are heard promptly, fairly and confidentially, by someone who has not been involved in the matter, and the employee may be accompanied as the Company's policy permits. Complaints of sexual harassment are dealt with under the Company's policy under the Sexual Harassment of Women at Workplace (Prevention, Prohibition and Redressal) Act, 2013 and not under this procedure.", "Raising a grievance in good faith will never be held against the employee. Knowingly false complaints may themselves lead to disciplinary action."], ["end", "records", "Records and review", "HR keeps a confidential record of each grievance, of the steps taken and of the outcome. {{input.policy_owner}} reviews the number and nature of grievances regularly and reports patterns to management so that causes are addressed. An employee who is not satisfied with the outcome may escalate to the next level in the table above within the time shown."]],
  "hr.referral": [["end", "process", "How to refer a candidate", "To make a referral, send the candidate's resume to HR through the Company's referral channel with your own name and employee code. HR confirms receipt, tells you whether the candidate is considered and keeps you informed of the outcome. The candidate goes through the same selection process as every other candidate, and a referral does not guarantee an interview or an offer.", "The reward is paid as the table above states, provided that the referred person joins, completes the period stated, and is not a person whom the exclusions above remove from the scheme. HR's decision on whether a referral qualifies is final, and the Company may amend or withdraw this scheme with notice."]],
