// ── Batch 3: management and operations ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Object.assign(EXPAND, {
  "mg.project_charter": [["after:budget", "governance", "Governance, assumptions and success", "The project is sponsored by {{input.sponsor}} and managed day to day by {{input.manager}}. The sponsor approves the charter, removes obstacles the manager cannot remove, and decides on any change to scope, budget or dates that goes beyond what the manager is authorised to approve. The manager reports progress and risks to the sponsor at the intervals agreed at kick-off.", "The project succeeds when the objectives above are met within the scope, the budget and the dates, and when the people who will use the result accept it. The key assumptions are that the people and funds described in this charter are available when needed and that the stakeholders listed take part as expected; if an assumption fails, the manager tells the sponsor at once."]],
  "mg.project_plan": [
    ["start", "overview", "Purpose and approach", "This plan describes how {{input.project_name}} will be delivered by {{input.manager}} and the team named below. It breaks the scope into work packages with an owner for each, sets the milestones against which progress is measured, shows who is working on the project and how much of their time it needs, and records the risks and how they will be handled. It is owned by {{input.owner}}.", "The plan is a living document. The project manager updates it whenever the scope, the dates, the team or the risks change, tells the stakeholders what has changed, and keeps earlier versions so that decisions can be traced."],
    ["end", "controls", "Monitoring, change control and closure", "Progress is tracked against the milestones above at every project status meeting, and the project manager reports any slippage, and the action being taken, to the sponsor without waiting for the next report. A change to the scope, the milestones or the team is recorded as a change request, assessed for its effect on time, cost and quality, and approved by the sponsor before it is built into the plan.", "The project is closed when the deliverables have been accepted by the people they were built for, the records and documents have been handed over, the team has met to record what was learned, and any open risks and issues have been passed to a named owner."],
  ],
  "mg.brd": [["end", "traceability", "Approval and change of requirements", "Each requirement above has a number so that it can be traced to the design, the tests and the acceptance of the result. A requirement may be added, changed or removed only through the change process agreed for the project, and only with the approval of the business owner; the effect of the change on cost, time and the other requirements is stated before it is approved. By signing, the approvers confirm that these requirements describe what the business needs and that the objectives above will be met if they are delivered."]],
  "mg.prd": [["end", "launch", "Launch, support and open questions", "Before release the team confirms that the features above meet their acceptance criteria, that the non-functional requirements have been tested, and that support, documentation and communications are ready. After release the team monitors the success metrics above, reviews them at agreed intervals and reports to the owner whether the product is meeting its goals.", "Questions that remain open at the date of this document are tracked by the owner, {{input.owner}}, who decides how each is resolved and updates this document accordingly. Requirements not marked as priorities may be moved to a later release if time or cost requires, with the owner's approval."]],
  "mg.status_report": [["start", "intro", "About this report", "This report gives {{client.name}} and the project's stakeholders an honest view of how {{input.project_name}} stands at the end of {{input.period}}, as prepared by {{input.owner}}. It reports the overall health of the project ({{input.health}}), what was achieved, what is at risk and what will be done next. Where the health is amber or red, the report states what is needed to bring it back on track and who must act."], ["end", "decisions", "Decisions and support needed", "Anything that needs a decision or help from the sponsor or the client is listed in the risks and next steps above, with the date by which it is needed. The next report will say whether each item has been resolved."]],
  "mg.weekly_report": [["start", "intro", "About this report", "This is the weekly report of the {{input.team}} team for {{input.week}}, prepared by {{input.owner}}. It shows what the team completed, what it plans to do next and what is getting in its way, so that managers can see progress without a meeting and can help where help is needed."], ["end", "notes", "How to read and use this report", "Items under \"done\" are complete and need no further action. Items under \"planned\" are the team's commitment for next week and may change if a blocker is not removed or a higher priority arrives. Blockers are listed with the support needed; if one is not resolved within a few days, the owner raises it with the next level of management, so that no blocker waits unseen. Please send any correction to {{input.owner}} before the report is shared more widely."]],
  "mg.board_report": [["start", "intro", "Introduction", "This report is presented to the Board by {{input.owner}} for {{input.period}}. It summarises the highlights of the period, the key figures, the financial and operational position, the main risks and the matters on which the Board's decision or guidance is sought. The figures are drawn from the Company's management accounts and operational records and are subject to the Company's normal review."], ["end", "governance", "Governance and compliance matters", "Matters of governance and compliance that the Board should note, such as statutory filings made or due, changes in directors or key managerial personnel, and material contracts entered into, are reported by the Company Secretary or the finance head with this report. The Board is asked to note the report and, where this report seeks resolutions, to consider them as set out above."]],
  "mg.mis_report": [["start", "intro", "About this report", "This management information report for {{input.period}} is prepared by {{input.owner}} to give management one consistent view of performance. It compares each key measure with its target, explains the main differences and lists the actions agreed to correct them, so that attention goes where it is needed.", "Each measure is calculated in the same way every period so that trends can be trusted. Where the definition or the source of a measure changes, the change is stated in this report."], ["end", "followup", "Follow-up", "Actions in the table above have an owner and a due date and are reviewed at the next management meeting. An action that is complete is closed with a note of what was done; an action that is overdue is escalated to the person who asked for it."]],
  "mg.kpi": [["start", "intro", "Purpose of this framework", "This framework defines how the performance of {{input.department}} is measured, so that everyone knows what good looks like and decisions are made on facts. It is owned by {{input.owner}} and is reviewed {{input.review_cycle}}.", "A good indicator is relevant to an objective, clearly defined, measurable from a reliable source, and within the control of the team accountable for it. Each indicator below therefore has a definition, a target and a frequency of measurement."], ["end", "rules", "Using the indicators", "Results are reported in the same format each period, compared with the target, and discussed by the owner and the team. An indicator that is consistently off target triggers a review of its causes and an agreed action. Indicators and targets are revisited at each review, and a change is recorded with its date and reason so that trends remain comparable."]],
  "mg.okr": [["start", "intro", "How to read this plan", "This plan sets the objectives and key results of the {{input.team}} team for {{input.quarter}}, prepared by {{input.owner}}. An objective says what the team wants to achieve; its key results say how the team will know. Objectives should be ambitious but clear, and key results should be measurable and time-bound, so that at the end of the quarter anyone can tell whether the result was achieved."]],
  "mg.minutes": [["start", "intro", "Meeting details", "Minutes of {{input.meeting}} held on {{input.meeting_date|date}} at {{input.venue}}, recorded by {{input.owner}}. The minutes record who attended, what was discussed, what was decided and who will do what by when. They are circulated to the attendees for correction and become the agreed record once approved at the next meeting."], ["end", "close", "Next meeting and approval", "Any matter not completed at this meeting is carried forward to the next. The minutes are confirmed as a correct record when the chair signs them at the following meeting, and any correction is noted in the minutes of that meeting."]],
  "mg.board_resolution": [["start", "intro", "Overview of the resolution", "This is a resolution of the Board of Directors of {{company.legal_name}} on the subject of {{input.subject}}, passed on {{input.meeting_date|date}} at {{input.venue}}, in accordance with the Companies Act, 2013 and the Company's articles of association. The Board considered the matter, the information placed before it and any declaration of interest, and resolved as set out below."]],
  "mg.change_request": [["start", "intro", "About this request", "This change request, reference {{input.reference}}, for {{input.project_name}} was raised by {{input.requested_by}} and is managed by {{input.owner}} for {{client.name}}. It describes the change proposed, why it is needed and what it would mean for cost and schedule, so that the approver can decide on complete information. No work on the change begins until it is approved in writing."], ["end", "decision", "Decision and implementation", "The approver records the decision, the date and any conditions below. An approved change is added to the project plan, and the baseline is updated with its cost and schedule effect. A rejected change is closed with the reason, and the requester is informed. If the change is approved with conditions, the project manager confirms in writing that each condition has been met before work starts."]],
  "mg.postmortem": [["start", "intro", "About this review", "This post-incident review of {{input.incident}}, which occurred on {{input.incident_date|date}} and lasted {{input.duration}}, is prepared by {{input.owner}}. Its purpose is to learn: to establish what happened, why it happened and what will change so that it does not happen again. It is blameless; it looks at systems, processes and decisions, and not at individuals."], ["end", "lessons", "What went well, what did not and follow-up", "The review records what helped the team to detect and resolve the incident, what slowed them down, and where the organisation was lucky. Every action above has an owner and a date, and the owner of this review checks at the dates agreed that each action is complete. Where an action cannot be done, the reason is recorded and the risk is accepted by a named person."]],
  "mg.business_plan": [["start", "intro", "About this plan", "This business plan is prepared by {{input.owner}} for {{company.name}}. It sets out the opportunity, the market, the strategy, how the business will operate and the financial plan, in order to guide decisions and to give lenders, investors and partners an honest picture of the business. Statements about the future are plans and not guarantees, and the assumptions behind them are stated."], ["end", "risks", "Risks, assumptions and next steps", "The plan rests on the assumptions stated in the sections above and in the financial notes. The main risks to it are changes in the market, in costs, in the availability of people and funds, and in the law, and management will monitor them and revise the plan when they change. The plan is reviewed at regular intervals, and the owner records the changes made and the reasons."]],
  "mg.strategy_memo": [["start", "intro", "Purpose of this memo", "This memo is prepared by {{input.owner}} for {{input.audience}} on the topic of {{input.topic}}. It sets out the context, the options that were considered with their advantages and disadvantages, and a recommendation, so that the reader can make a decision. It is written to be read in a few minutes and to stand on its own, with enough background that the reader does not need to ask for anything else before deciding. Figures, where used, come from the sources named in the sections that follow."], ["end", "next", "Decision required and next steps", "The reader is asked to decide whether to accept the recommendation, choose another option, or ask for further work. If the recommendation is accepted, the owner will prepare a plan with responsibilities and dates and will report progress at the interval the reader prefers."]],
  "mg.circular": [["start", "heading", "Circular details", "Circular on {{input.subject}}, issued by {{company.name}} and applicable to {{input.applies_to}} with effect from {{input.effective_date|date}}."], ["end", "compliance", "Compliance and queries", "This circular is binding on everyone it applies to from the date stated, and supersedes any earlier instruction on the same subject to the extent they differ. Managers are asked to make sure that their teams have read and understood it. Any question about its meaning should be sent to {{input.contact}}, who will clarify it in writing where the question is of general interest. A circular remains in force until it is withdrawn or replaced by a later circular, and employees who join after it is issued are made aware of it as part of their induction. Display copies are placed where employees can reach them."]],
  "mg.doa": [["start", "purpose", "Purpose and scope", "This delegation of authority sets out who may approve what, up to which limit and under which conditions, in {{company.name}}, so that decisions are taken at the right level, spending is controlled and responsibility is clear. It applies to every employee and to every transaction in the areas listed in the matrix below, and it is owned by {{input.owner}} with effect from {{input.effective_date|date}}."], ["end", "principles", "Principles of application", "A person may not approve a transaction in which they have a personal interest, or one that they have initiated themselves. An approval limit applies to the total value of a transaction, and a transaction may not be split to bring it within a lower limit. Where a delegate is absent, the authority passes to the person named by the Board or the managing director, and not by the delegate. Approvals are recorded in writing, and exceptions need the written approval of the next higher authority."]],
  "mg.org_chart": [["end", "notes", "Notes", "The structure and the reporting lines are those in force on {{input.as_on|date}}. A change in the structure takes effect only when it has been approved and communicated by HR, after which this document is updated by {{input.owner}}. The strength shown is the number of approved positions in each department at that date and not a count of vacancies."]],
  "op.sop": [["start", "intro", "Document control and use", "This standard operating procedure for {{input.process}} in {{input.department}} is owned by {{input.owner}} and applies from {{input.effective_date|date}}. It tells everyone who does this work what to do, in what order, who is responsible and what to record, so that the process gives the same result whoever carries it out.", "Staff must follow the current approved version. A printed copy is not controlled. Suggestions for improvement are sent to the owner, who reviews them and issues a revised version when a change is approved."], ["end", "records", "Records, review and training", "Records created by this procedure are kept for the period the Company's retention policy states and are available for audit. The procedure is reviewed at regular intervals and whenever the process, the tools or the law change. New staff are trained on it before they carry out the process on their own, and the training is recorded."]],
  "op.work_instruction": [["end", "safety", "Safety, quality and reporting", "Follow every step in the order shown and complete each check before moving on. If a step cannot be done as written, or if anything looks unsafe or unusual, stop and tell {{input.owner}} before continuing. Any defect, near miss or injury must be reported straight away, and the work must not resume until the cause has been understood."]],
  "op.incident_report": [["start", "intro", "About this report", "This incident report records {{input.incident}}, which took place on {{input.incident_date|date}} at {{input.location}}, as reported by {{input.reported_by}} and compiled by {{input.owner}}. It is completed as soon as possible after the event, while facts are fresh, and it states what is known and what is not, without opinion or blame."], ["end", "followup", "Investigation and follow-up", "The owner of this report decides whether the incident needs a fuller investigation, informs the people who need to know, and, where the law requires it, notifies the authority concerned within the time the law allows. Each action above is tracked to completion, and the report is closed only when the owner is satisfied that the cause has been dealt with. The report is kept as a confidential record and is shared only with those who need it to act or to learn from it."]],
  "op.bcp": [["start", "intro", "Purpose and objectives", "This business continuity plan sets out how {{company.name}} will keep its critical activities going, or restore them quickly, if a disruption occurs. It is owned by {{input.owner}} and takes effect from {{input.effective_date|date}}. Its objectives are to protect people first, to restore critical functions within the recovery targets below, to communicate clearly with staff, customers and others who depend on us, and to learn from every disruption."], ["after:recovery", "activation", "Activation, communication and roles", "The plan is activated by the owner, or by the person acting for the owner, when a disruption threatens a critical function and cannot be handled within normal procedures. On activation, the owner informs the people listed in the contact table, assigns the recovery tasks to the function owners, and keeps a log of decisions and times. Messages to staff, customers and other stakeholders are given by one named spokesperson so that information is consistent and accurate."], ["end", "testing", "Testing, maintenance and review", "The plan is tested at regular intervals through exercises that involve the people who would carry it out, and the results and the lessons are recorded. The plan, the contact details and the recovery strategies are reviewed after every exercise and every real disruption, whenever the business or its systems change significantly, and otherwise at least once a year. The owner keeps a copy of the plan available offline so that it can be used when systems are not."]],
  "op.quality_manual": [["start", "intro", "Introduction and scope", "This quality manual describes the quality management system of {{company.name}}, which is built to meet {{input.standards}}. It is owned by {{input.owner}} and applies from {{input.effective_date|date}}. It describes how the Company understands its customers' needs, plans and controls its work, measures results and improves, and it gives the reader a map to the documents and records that make up the system."], ["after:processes", "responsibilities", "Management responsibility and resources", "Top management is responsible for the quality policy, for making sure that the quality objectives are set and reviewed, for providing the people, infrastructure and information the system needs, and for reviewing the system at planned intervals. Every employee is responsible for the quality of their own work, for following the procedures that apply to it, and for reporting any nonconformity and suggesting improvements."], ["after:audit", "improvement", "Control of documents, nonconformity and improvement", "Documents of the system are approved before issue, identified by version, kept up to date and withdrawn when obsolete. Records are kept as evidence that work has been done as planned, and are protected from loss and unauthorised change. A nonconformity is corrected, its cause is investigated, and action is taken to stop it recurring; the action is checked for effectiveness. The system is audited internally {{input.audit_cycle}}, and results are reviewed by management so that the system is improved continually. Customer feedback and complaints are recorded and used as an input to that review."]],
  "op.hse_policy": [["end", "responsibilities", "Responsibilities, training and review", "Every employee must follow safe working practices, use the protective equipment provided, report hazards, incidents and near misses at once, and not do work for which they are not trained. Managers must make sure that risks in their areas are assessed, that controls are in place, that people are trained, and that incidents are investigated and their causes put right. Contractors and visitors who work on our sites must follow the same rules.", "This policy is owned by {{input.owner}}, applies from {{input.effective_date|date}}, and is reviewed at regular intervals and after any serious incident. The Company complies with the health and safety laws that apply to its sites, and it consults employees on matters that affect their safety."]],
  "op.visitor_policy": [["start", "purpose", "Purpose and scope", "This policy protects the people, property and information at {{company.name}}'s premises by controlling who enters and why. It applies to everyone who is not an employee and who comes to the premises, including guests, contractors, delivery staff and candidates, and to every employee who invites or meets them. It is owned by {{input.owner}} and takes effect from {{input.effective_date|date}}."], ["end", "responsibilities", "Responsibilities and records", "The reception, at {{input.reception}}, registers every visitor, checks identification, issues a pass and tells the host. Hosts are responsible for their visitors throughout the visit and must escort them outside meeting areas. Visitors must wear their pass, follow safety and security instructions and sign out when they leave. Visitor records contain personal data and are kept only as long as needed for security and safety, and then deleted, in line with the Company's data protection obligations."]],
  "op.handover": [["start", "intro", "Purpose of this handover", "This note records the handover of responsibilities from {{input.from}} to {{input.to}} on {{input.handover_date|date}}, prepared by {{input.owner}}. It lets the person taking over continue the work without interruption by stating what is in progress, what is pending and who to contact, so that nothing is lost when responsibility changes hands."], ["end", "confirm", "Confirmation", "By taking over, the receiving person confirms that they have understood the status and the pending items above, have been given access to the information and tools they need, and know who to ask for help. The person handing over remains available for questions for the period the manager agrees."]],
});

/** Adds sections to a template that already has entries above. */
function more(id: string, ...adds: (Add | Add[])[]): void { EXPAND[id] = [...(EXPAND[id] ?? []), ...adds.flatMap((a) => (Array.isArray(a[0]) ? (a as Add[]) : [a as Add]))]; }

more("mg.mis_report", ["end", "definitions", "Definitions and data sources", "Each measure in this report has a written definition and a named data source, and is taken from the same source every period. The owner of each measure is responsible for the accuracy of its figure, and corrections to earlier figures are shown openly with the reason."]);
more("mg.change_request", ["end", "assessment", "Assessment and approval criteria", "The approver considers whether the change is needed to meet the objectives of the project, whether its cost and schedule effect are acceptable, whether the risk it introduces is understood and controlled, and whether the change can be tested before it is accepted."]);
more("mg.strategy_memo", ["end", "criteria", "How the options were judged", "The options were judged against their fit with the objectives of the business, their cost and the effort they need, the risk they carry and how reversible they are. Where the evidence is incomplete, the memo says so, and the recommendation states what would change it."]);
more("mg.circular", ["end", "validity", "Validity", "This circular remains in force until it is withdrawn or replaced by a later circular. Display copies are placed where employees can see them, and employees who join later are told of it during induction."]);
more("op.quality_manual", ["end", "customer", "Customer focus and feedback", "The Company listens to its customers, records their feedback and complaints, and uses them as an input to management review so that the system improves where customers feel it most."]);

// ── Batch 4: IT, vendor, pre-sale, finance ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
more("it.security_policy", ["end", "awareness", "Awareness and review", "Everyone covered by this policy receives security awareness training when they join and at regular intervals, and is told promptly of changes that affect them. The policy is reviewed by {{input.owner}} at planned intervals and after any significant incident."]);
more("it.password", ["after:policy", "guidance", "Guidance for users and administrators", "Passwords and other credentials are personal. They must not be shared, written where others can see them, sent by e-mail or message, or reused for accounts outside the Company. Users should choose a passphrase that is easy to remember and hard to guess, use the password manager the Company provides, and change a credential at once if they suspect it has been exposed.", "Administrators must protect privileged accounts with stronger controls, must never use a privileged account for everyday work, and must change vendor default credentials before a system is used. Systems must store credentials only in a protected form, lock an account after repeated failed attempts, and record sign-ins so that misuse can be detected. Any suspected compromise is reported to {{input.owner}} immediately.", "This policy is owned by {{input.owner}} and takes effect from {{input.effective_date|date}}. An exception needs the owner's written approval and is recorded with the reason and the date on which it ends."]);
more("it.access", ["end", "responsibilities", "Responsibilities and review", "Managers request access for their people only to the extent the job needs it, and confirm every year that it is still needed. System owners approve access to their systems and keep a record of who has it. IT grants, changes and removes access as approved, and removes it on the day a person leaves or changes role. Every user is responsible for what is done with their account.", "Access is reviewed every {{input.review_months}} months and the results are recorded. This policy is owned by {{input.owner}} and applies from {{input.effective_date|date}}."]);
more("it.byod", ["end", "support", "Support, privacy and review", "The Company supports work use of a personal device only as far as access to Company systems is concerned and is not responsible for the device itself or for personal data on it. The Company's controls apply only to the work data and the work applications on the device; the Company does not read personal messages, photographs or files, but it may remove work data if the device is lost, if the employee leaves, or if the employee does not follow this policy. This policy is owned by {{input.owner}} and applies from {{input.effective_date|date}}."]);
more("it.backup_dr", [
  ["start", "purpose", "Purpose and scope", "This policy makes sure that the data and systems {{company.name}} depends on can be restored after loss, damage or disruption. It covers the systems listed in the table below, the way they are backed up, how quickly they must be recovered (the recovery time objective) and how much data may be lost (the recovery point objective). It is owned by {{input.owner}} and takes effect from {{input.effective_date|date}}."],
  ["end", "responsibilities", "Responsibilities and controls", "System owners decide, with IT, how important each system is and what recovery objectives it needs. IT configures and monitors the backups, checks every day that jobs have completed, fixes failures at once and reports repeated failures to the owner. Backups are encrypted, kept in a location separate from the system they protect, and protected from deletion by unauthorised people.", "A backup that has never been restored cannot be trusted. Restores are therefore tested {{input.test_cycle}}, the results are recorded, and any failure is corrected and retested. Backups are kept for the period the Company's retention policy and the law require and are then securely destroyed."],
  ["end", "disaster", "Disaster recovery process", "In a disaster, the owner declares recovery, informs the people named in the continuity plan, and directs IT to restore systems in the order of their importance. IT keeps a log of what is restored and when, tests each system before it is handed back, and tells the owner when service has returned. After the event, the owner reviews what happened, how the objectives were met and what must change in this policy and in the backups."],
]);
more("it.incident_response", ["end", "preparation", "Roles, evidence and lessons learned", "The incident response team meets the roles in the table above, and one person leads each incident and keeps a written log of the time, the facts and the decisions. Evidence such as logs, images and messages is preserved in a way that keeps it reliable, and systems are not wiped until the lead agrees. Communication with staff, customers, regulators and the press is only made by the people the lead names.", "After every incident, the team meets to review what happened, how quickly it was found and contained, what worked and what did not, and records improvements with owners and dates. Where personal data is involved, the Company assesses its obligations under the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 and other applicable law, and informs those who must be informed within the time the law requires. This plan is owned by {{input.owner}} and takes effect from {{input.effective_date|date}}."]);
more("it.change_mgmt", ["start", "purpose", "Purpose and scope", "This policy makes sure that changes to {{company.name}}'s systems and services are planned, assessed, approved, tested and recorded, so that they do not cause avoidable outages or security weaknesses. It applies to every change to production systems, networks, applications and configurations, whoever makes it, and is owned by {{input.owner}} with effect from {{input.effective_date|date}}."], ["end", "controls", "Controls, emergency changes and records", "Every change has a written request that states what will change, why, the risk, the test result and how to undo it, and is approved by the approver for its kind before it is made. Changes are made in the agreed window by someone other than the approver, and are checked afterwards.", "An emergency change that cannot wait for approval may be made by the on-call engineer to restore service, and is reported to the owner at once and approved afterwards. Every change, including emergency changes, is recorded, and the records are reviewed regularly so that repeat problems are found and removed."]);
more("it.data_classification", [["start", "purpose", "Purpose and scope", "This policy sets how {{company.name}} labels its information according to its sensitivity, so that everyone knows how to handle it. It applies to all information the Company creates, receives or stores, in any form, and to everyone who handles it. It is owned by {{input.owner}} and applies from {{input.effective_date|date}}."], ["end", "responsibilities", "Responsibilities and review", "Every information owner is responsible for classifying the information they own at the time it is created or received, and for reviewing the classification when its sensitivity changes. Information that has not been classified is treated as the level next above the lowest until its owner decides. Every user must handle information as its classification requires, must not lower a classification without the owner's approval, and must report any loss or unauthorised disclosure at once.", "Personal data is handled in line with the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 and the Company's privacy policy as well as with the rules for its class. This policy is reviewed at regular intervals and after a significant incident."]]);
more("it.asset_policy", ["end", "responsibilities", "Responsibilities and lifecycle", "IT keeps a register of every asset with its owner, location and status, from purchase to disposal. Employees are responsible for the assets issued to them: they must use them for work, protect them from loss and damage, report any loss or theft at once, and return them as the policy says. Before any asset is reused, sold or disposed of, its data is securely erased and the erasure is recorded. This policy is owned by {{input.owner}} and applies from {{input.effective_date|date}}."]);
more("it.sdlc", ["start", "purpose", "Purpose and scope", "This policy makes security part of the way {{company.name}} designs, builds, tests and releases software, so that weaknesses are prevented early and not found by attackers. It applies to everyone who develops or changes software for the Company, including contractors, and is owned by {{input.owner}} with effect from {{input.effective_date|date}}."], ["end", "controls", "Controls through the lifecycle", "Security requirements are agreed at the design stage, and threats are considered before building starts. Code is reviewed by a second person before it is merged, third-party components are checked and kept up to date, secrets are never stored in source code, and automated tests and security scans run before release. Test data does not contain real personal data unless it is protected as production data is. Releases are approved, recorded and can be reversed, and vulnerabilities found after release are fixed in order of their risk."]);
more("it.vendor_security", ["end", "use", "How the answers are used", "The answers to this questionnaire are used by {{input.owner}} to assess the risk of working with {{vendor.name}} and to decide what safeguards are needed in the contract, such as limits on access, audit rights and the notification of incidents. Please answer every question honestly and completely and attach evidence where you can. If a question does not apply, explain why. The information you give is treated as confidential and is used only for this assessment."]);
more("it.runbook", [["start", "purpose", "Purpose and use", "This runbook describes how to operate and recover {{input.system}}, written for the engineer who is on call and may not have worked on it before. It is owned by {{input.owner}}. Follow the procedures in order, record what you do and when, and escalate to the owner if you are unsure or if a step does not give the result described."], ["end", "escalation", "Escalation and after the incident", "If the problem is not solved within the time the severity allows, or if data may be at risk, escalate to {{input.owner}} and follow the incident response plan. After the incident, record what happened and what you did, and update this runbook with anything that was missing or wrong, so that the next person has a better guide."]]);
more("it.release_notes", [["start", "intro", "About this release", "These release notes describe version {{input.version}} of {{input.product}}, released on {{input.release_date|date}}. They list what is new, what has changed and what is known to be wrong, so that users and support teams can decide when and how to upgrade and what to expect."], ["end", "upgrade", "Upgrading and support", "Before upgrading, read the changes and known issues above and take a backup where the product holds data. If you find a problem that is not listed, report it to support with the version number and the steps that led to it. Customers using an earlier version should follow the upgrade guidance supplied with the product."]]);
more("it.srs", [["start", "purpose", "Purpose and scope", "This software requirements specification, prepared by {{input.owner}} for {{client.name}}, describes what {{input.product}} must do and the conditions it must meet. It is the agreement between the people who need the software and the people who build it about what will be delivered, and it is the basis for design, testing and acceptance."], ["end", "quality", "Quality attributes, acceptance and change", "Besides its functions, the software must meet the quality requirements that the stakeholders agree, such as performance, availability, security, usability and maintainability, each stated so that it can be tested. The software is accepted when each requirement above has been shown, by test or inspection, to be met. A requirement may be added, changed or removed only through the change process agreed between the parties, and its effect on cost and time is stated before it is approved."]]);
more("vn.evaluation", ["start", "intro", "How the evaluation is done", "This scorecard compares the vendors being considered for {{input.requirement}}, evaluated on {{input.evaluated_on|date}} by {{input.owner}}. Each criterion has a weight that reflects its importance and was agreed before the proposals were opened. Every evaluator scores each vendor independently against the same criteria, and writes a reason for each score, so that the result can be explained and defended."]);
more("vn.rejection", ["end", "close", "Closing", "We appreciate the time and effort you spent on your proposal and the interest you have shown in working with {{company.name}}. This decision does not prevent you from taking part in future requests, and we will keep your details on our records only for the purpose and the period our policy allows."]);
more("vn.payment_terms", ["end", "general", "General terms", "Payment is made against a correct invoice that quotes the purchase order, and the period for payment runs from the date the Company receives it. Disputed items are notified within a reasonable time, and the undisputed part is paid on time. The Company may set off amounts the Vendor owes it, and tax is deducted at source where the law requires, with a certificate given to the Vendor. These terms apply to every order unless a written agreement says otherwise."]);
more("vn.code_of_conduct", ["start", "purpose", "Purpose and scope", "This code sets out the standards of conduct {{company.name}} expects from every vendor, supplier and contractor that works with it, and from their staff and subcontractors. It applies to everything a vendor does for the Company or on its premises, and acceptance of this code is a condition of doing business with us."]);
more("vn.performance", [["start", "intro", "About this review", "This review of {{vendor.name}} covers {{input.period}} and is prepared by {{input.owner}}. It scores the vendor against agreed measures such as quality, delivery, responsiveness and compliance, records the issues that arose and agrees actions, so that the relationship is managed on evidence and decisions about the vendor's future are fair."], ["end", "outcome", "Outcome and follow-up", "The result of the review is shared with the vendor, who is invited to respond. Actions have an owner and a date and are checked at the next review. A vendor with a poor result is placed on a corrective plan; one with a good result may be considered for more work. The Company may reduce, suspend or end the relationship where improvement does not follow, as the contract allows."]]);
more("ps.quotation", [["start", "summary", "Summary of the quotation", "This quotation is prepared by {{company.legal_name}} for {{client.name}} and describes the goods or services offered, the price and the terms on which they are offered. It is valid for the period stated and is based on the information the client has given us."], ["end", "quote_terms", "Terms of the quotation", "Prices are exclusive of taxes unless stated. The quotation is an offer that the client may accept in writing within its validity; acceptance forms a contract on the terms stated here and in any written agreement the parties sign. We may revise the price if the client changes the requirement or if the quantities differ from those quoted."]]);
more("ps.estimate", [["start", "intro", "About this estimate", "This estimate, prepared by {{input.owner}} for {{client.name}}, gives the effort we expect {{input.title}} to need. It is an estimate and not a fixed price or a commitment, and it is based on the scope and the assumptions in this document, which the client should read carefully."], ["end", "next", "How the estimate is used", "If the client wishes to proceed, we will prepare a proposal or a statement of work that fixes the scope, the price and the timeline. If the scope changes, we will revise the estimate and tell the client what the change would do to the effort."]]);
more("ps.pitch_outline", [["end", "story", "Telling the story", "A strong pitch follows a simple path: the problem the audience has, why it matters now, the solution, the evidence that it works, the plan and the ask. Open with the audience's problem and not with the company's history. Use one idea per slide, show evidence instead of claiming it, rehearse the timing, and end with a clear request that makes it easy for the audience to say yes."]]);
more("ps.capability", [["start", "intro", "Introduction", "This capability statement presents {{company.legal_name}} to buyers, partners and evaluators: what we do, what we have done and how to reach us. It is written to be read in a few minutes and to support a decision to work with us."], ["end", "contact_more", "Why work with us", "We aim to be a dependable partner: we say clearly what we can and cannot do, we deliver what we promise and we are open about problems. We are happy to provide references, to meet the people who would work on your account and to answer any question about our credentials."]]);
more("ps.case_study", [["start", "intro", "At a glance", "This case study describes how {{company.name}} worked with {{input.client_name}}, a business in the {{input.industry}} sector. It follows the story from the client's challenge to the solution and the results, so that readers in a similar position can see what is possible."], ["end", "quote", "Lessons and next steps", "Every project teaches something. The lessons from this work have shaped how we approach similar problems, and the client continues to be a valued relationship. If your organisation faces a similar challenge, we would be glad to discuss how our experience can help you."]]);
more("ps.discovery", [["start", "intro", "About this discovery", "This record of a requirement discovery meeting with {{client.name}}, held on {{input.meeting_date|date}} and led by {{input.owner}}, captures what we learned about the client's situation, needs and constraints. It is written so that the client can confirm it is right, and so that any proposal that follows is based on what was actually said."], ["end", "confirm", "Confirming this record", "The client is asked to read this record and to tell us of any error or omission. Until the client confirms it, any proposal we prepare will state the assumptions we have made. The next steps above have owners and dates, and progress on them will be shared with the client."]]);
more("ps.rfp_response", [["end", "terms", "Terms and validity", "This response is submitted in answer to the request for proposal {{input.rfp_title}} and is valid for {{input.validity_days}} days from the date of submission. It is based on the requirements in the request and on any clarifications issued in writing. Our price is stated in the pricing section and is exclusive of taxes unless it says otherwise. We are willing to discuss our response and to clarify any part of it."]]);
more("ps.solution_brief", [["start", "intro", "Overview", "This solution brief prepared by {{input.owner}} for {{client.name}} describes {{input.solution}} in plain terms: the problem it addresses, how it works and the benefits it gives. It is intended to help decision makers understand the proposal quickly and to decide whether to explore it further."], ["end", "next", "Next steps", "If the brief matches your need, the next step is a short conversation to confirm your requirements, followed by a detailed proposal with scope, price and timeline. We will be glad to arrange a demonstration or to introduce you to a customer who uses the solution."]]);
more("ps.followup", ["end", "next", "Next steps", "Thank you for taking the time to meet us. As agreed, we will send the information we promised and will contact you on the date we suggested to hear your thoughts. If there is anything else that would help your decision, please tell us and we will be glad to provide it. We look forward to the opportunity to work with you."]);
more("ps.demo_plan", [["start", "intro", "Purpose of the demonstration", "This plan for the demonstration for {{client.name}} on {{input.demo_date|date}}, prepared by {{input.owner}}, sets out what will be shown, who will attend and how success will be judged. It is shared with the client in advance so that the session answers the questions that matter to them and uses their time well."], ["end", "logistics", "Preparation and follow-up", "Before the session we check the environment, the data and the access of every participant, and agree what the client will provide. After it we send a short summary of what was shown, the questions raised and the agreed next steps, within the time we have promised."]]);
more("fn.proforma", ["end", "terms", "Terms", "This proforma invoice is issued for the purpose of payment in advance, customs, or approval, and is not a tax invoice. A tax invoice will be issued when the goods or services are supplied and payment is received as the law requires. Prices are valid for the period stated on this document."]);
more("fn.credit_note", ["end", "notes", "Notes", "This credit note reduces the amount due on the invoice it refers to, for the reason stated above, and any tax adjustment follows the law applicable to the original supply. It will be set off against your next invoice unless you ask us in writing to refund it."]);
more("fn.payment_reminder", [["end", "next", "How to pay and what to do next", "Please pay the outstanding amount using the payment details on the invoice and quote the invoice number, so that we can match your payment promptly. If you have already paid, please send us the payment details and accept our thanks. If there is a query about the invoice, please contact our accounts team straight away so that we can resolve it. We value your business and would like to keep our records in order."]]);
more("fn.expense_policy", ["end", "responsibilities", "Responsibilities and review", "Employees are responsible for spending as little as is reasonable, for keeping proof of every expense and for claiming within the time this policy allows. Managers approve only expenses that are for business and within policy. Finance checks each claim against policy, tax rules and proof before paying it. Claims that are false or inflated may lead to disciplinary action and recovery of the amount. This policy is reviewed regularly, and exceptions need written approval from the finance head."]);
more("fn.travel_policy", [["start", "purpose", "Purpose and scope", "This policy sets the rules for business travel by employees of {{company.name}}: when travel is approved, what the Company pays for and how expenses are claimed. Its aim is that employees can travel safely and comfortably for business and that costs are reasonable and controlled. It applies to all employees and to anyone travelling on the Company's behalf."], ["end", "rules", "Approval, booking, safety and claims", "Travel must be approved by the manager before it is booked, and bookings are made through the channel Finance specifies so that the best available fare and the Company's discounts are used. Employees choose the class, accommodation and local transport the policy allows, and keep every bill and ticket. The Company expects employees to look after their safety, to tell their manager of changes in plan and to report any incident. Claims are made after the trip, with proof, in line with the expense policy, and advances are settled within the time that policy gives."]]);
more("fn.reimbursement", ["end", "note", "Declaration", "I declare that the expenses above were incurred for the Company's business, that the amounts are correct, that I have attached the proof for each, and that I have not claimed them elsewhere."]);
more("fn.budget_proposal", [["start", "intro", "Purpose of the proposal", "This budget proposal, prepared by {{input.owner}} for {{input.department}} for {{input.period}}, asks for funds to be approved for the items listed. It gives the amount for each item and the total, and explains the need, so that the approver can decide on the merits of each request and compare it with the benefits expected."], ["end", "approval", "Approval and control", "Funds are released only after approval, and spending is tracked against the approved figures. A change of more than the tolerance the finance head allows needs a fresh approval. The department head reports actual against budget at the intervals Finance sets, and unspent funds are returned at the end of the period unless approved otherwise."]]);

// ── Top-ups to reach the standard ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
more("it.change_mgmt", ["end", "review", "Review of changes", "Changes are reviewed after they are made. A change that caused an incident is analysed, and what is learned is used to improve the approval and testing steps in this policy."]);
more("it.data_classification", ["end", "labels", "Labelling and sharing", "Documents and systems carry their classification in a visible label wherever the format allows, and information is shared outside the Company only at the level its classification permits and, for more sensitive information, under a written confidentiality agreement."]);
more("it.asset_policy", ["end", "loss", "Loss, theft and misuse", "An employee who loses an asset or finds that it has been stolen must report it to IT and the manager at once, and, where the law or the Company's insurer requires it, to the police. IT will lock or wipe the device remotely where it can. An asset must not be used for anything unlawful, and use of an asset that breaks this policy may lead to action under the Company's disciplinary procedure."]);
more("it.sdlc", ["end", "exceptions", "Exceptions and review", "A release that cannot meet a control needs the written approval of the owner, who records the risk accepted and the date by which it will be removed. This policy is reviewed regularly as tools and threats change."]);
more("it.vendor_security", ["end", "evidence", "Evidence and updates", "Where you hold a certification or an independent audit report that covers a question, please attach it or give its reference. If your answers change, or if you have a security incident that affects our information, you must tell us promptly."]);
more("it.runbook", ["end", "contacts", "Ownership and maintenance", "This runbook is maintained by {{input.owner}} and reviewed after every incident and every significant change to {{input.system}}. An engineer who finds an error should correct it or tell the owner at once, because a wrong runbook is worse than none."]);
more("it.release_notes", ["end", "support2", "Compatibility and documentation", "Please check that your environment meets the requirements for {{input.product}} {{input.version}} before upgrading, and read the product documentation for changes in behaviour that may affect your own configuration or integrations."]);
more("it.srs", ["end", "glossary", "Definitions and references", "Terms with a special meaning in this specification are defined when they are first used, and documents it depends on, such as contracts, standards and interface descriptions, are listed so that readers know where to find them."]);
more("vn.code_of_conduct", ["end", "compliance", "Compliance, review and reporting", "A vendor must comply with the laws that apply to its business, including those on labour, safety, the environment, anti-corruption and data protection, and must tell the Company promptly of any breach of this code. The Company may ask for evidence of compliance and may audit it, and a serious or repeated breach may lead to the end of the relationship. Concerns can be raised in confidence with the Company's procurement or compliance team without fear of retaliation."]);
more("vn.performance", ["end", "scale", "Scoring method", "Each measure is scored on the same scale for every vendor, with the criteria agreed in advance, so that scores can be compared over time and between vendors, and any score that differs sharply from the previous period is explained."]);
more("ps.estimate", ["end", "validity", "Validity", "This estimate reflects our understanding at the date of issue and remains valid for a reasonable period. If the requirements, the team or the timing change, the estimate may change, and we will tell you before it affects you."]);
more("ps.pitch_outline", ["end", "slides", "Structure of the deck", "A deck of the length planned should open with the title and the problem, move through the solution, evidence and plan, and close with the ask and contact details, with any detail kept in an appendix for questions."]);
more("ps.capability", ["end", "evidence", "Evidence of capability", "Our claims are supported by the credentials and the projects listed above. We are glad to provide references from clients and to arrange a visit or a call with the people who would do the work."]);
more("ps.case_study", ["end", "approval", "Approval and use", "This case study is used with the approval of the client named in it. Figures are those the client has agreed may be shared, and nothing in it should be read as a promise of the same result for another client."]);
more("ps.discovery", ["end", "attendees_note", "Participants and confidentiality", "The people who attended are recorded above. What was discussed is confidential to the client and to us and is used only to prepare our response."]);
more("ps.rfp_response", ["end", "contact", "Clarifications and contact", "Please send any question about this response to our contact named in the cover letter, and we will answer promptly and in writing. We are willing to attend a presentation or to provide further information if you wish."]);
more("ps.solution_brief", ["end", "fit", "Is it right for you?", "The solution suits organisations that have the problem described above and that are ready to change how they work to solve it. We will tell you honestly if we believe another approach would serve you better."]);
more("ps.followup", ["end", "contact", "Contact", "If you would like to talk before then, please call or write to us at any time; we will gladly make time."]);
more("ps.demo_plan", ["end", "roles", "Roles on the day", "One person leads the demonstration, another handles questions and notes, and a third supports with the technical setup, so that the session runs smoothly and every question is recorded."]);
more("fn.expense_policy", ["end", "limits_advances", "Limits, advances and exceptions", "Limits for each category of expense are those the Company publishes and updates; employees must not split an expense to bring it within a limit. An advance is settled by a claim within the time stated, and an unsettled advance may be recovered from salary as the law permits."]);
more("fn.travel_policy", ["end", "emergencies", "Emergencies and changes", "If a trip must change, employees tell their manager and Finance, and an expense above what the policy allows needs approval afterwards with the reason. In an emergency, the employee's safety comes first and the Company will help."]);
more("fn.budget_proposal", ["end", "benefits", "Expected benefits and alternatives", "The proposal should state what the organisation will gain, how it will be measured, and what alternatives were considered, including doing nothing, so that the approver can see why this use of funds is the right one."]);

// ── Batch 5: training, marketing, legal; remaining top-ups ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
more("it.data_classification", ["end", "incidents", "Reporting", "Anyone who finds information that is wrongly labelled, wrongly shared or lost must report it to {{input.owner}} at once, so that the Company can limit harm and meet any duty to inform the people affected."]);
more("it.release_notes", ["end", "feedback", "Feedback", "We welcome your feedback on this release. Please tell us what works, what does not and what you would like next, and include the version number so that we can respond quickly."]);
more("ps.pitch_outline", ["end", "ask", "The ask", "End the pitch with one clear request: what you want the audience to do, by when, and what happens next if they agree. A pitch that does not ask for anything leaves the audience unsure how to respond."]);
more("ps.capability", ["end", "values", "How we work", "We work in the open: we agree scope and price before we start, we report progress regularly and we correct mistakes quickly. We treat our clients' information as confidential, and we follow the laws and standards that apply to our work."]);
more("ps.rfp_response", ["end", "compliance", "Statement of compliance", "We confirm that we have read the request for proposal and that this response addresses each of its requirements. Where we cannot fully meet a requirement, we have said so and explained how we propose to deal with it."]);
more("ps.demo_plan", ["end", "followup2", "Questions and open items", "Questions that we cannot answer during the session are noted and answered in writing afterwards, with a named owner and a date for each answer."]);
more("fn.travel_policy", ["end", "records", "Records and audit", "Finance keeps travel records and may audit them. Misuse of travel benefits may lead to recovery of the amount and to disciplinary action, after the employee has been heard."]);
more("tr.needs", [["start", "intro", "Purpose and method", "This training needs analysis for {{input.dept}} identifies the gap between the skills the work needs and the skills people have today, so that training time and money go where they will make most difference. It uses the evidence described below, not opinion alone, and it is reviewed {{input.next_review}}."], ["end", "approval", "Using this analysis", "The department head reviews the priorities above with HR, who prepare the training plan and budget. Training that does not address a gap in this analysis needs a reason. The effect of training is checked afterwards against the gaps it was meant to close, and the analysis is updated with what is learned."]]);
more("tr.plan", [["start", "intro", "Purpose of the plan", "This plan sets out how {{input.programme}} will be delivered to {{input.audience}} between {{input.start_date|date}} and {{input.end_date|date}}: what it aims to achieve, when each session takes place, who delivers it and what it costs. It gives the sponsor, the trainers and the participants a single reference for what to expect."], ["end", "evaluation", "Evaluation and responsibilities", "Participants give feedback after each session, and learning is checked as the course design says. HR is responsible for logistics, attendance records and the budget; trainers are responsible for content, delivery and assessment; line managers are responsible for releasing people to attend and for supporting them to use what they learn. Results and costs are reported to the sponsor after the programme ends."]]);
more("tr.curriculum", [["start", "intro", "About this course", "This curriculum describes {{input.course}}, a {{input.level}} course of {{input.hours}} hours. It states who the course is for, what learners must know beforehand ({{input.prerequisites}}), how the modules build on each other and what learners will be able to do at the end. It is the standard from which each batch of the course is planned and assessed."], ["end", "delivery", "Delivery, assessment and review", "Each module is delivered in the mode shown, using examples from the learners' own work wherever possible. Learners are assessed on what they can do and not on what they remember, and a learner who does not yet meet the standard is given support and a further attempt. The curriculum is reviewed after each batch using learner feedback and results, and updated when the content or the needs of the business change."]]);
more("tr.lesson_plan", [["start", "intro", "About this session", "This lesson plan for {{input.topic}} is prepared by {{input.trainer}} for a session of {{input.duration}} minutes. It shows what learners should be able to do afterwards, how the time is used and how the trainer will check understanding, so that the session is focused and any trainer could deliver it."], ["end", "prep", "Preparation and follow-up", "Before the session the trainer prepares the materials and the room, tests any equipment and reads the learners' background. After it the trainer records what worked and what did not, notes any learner who needs support, and updates this plan so that the next session is better."]]);
more("tr.material", [["start", "about", "About this material", "This material on {{input.topic}} is written for {{input.audience}}. It can be read alone or used in a session with a trainer. It explains the ideas in plain language, gives examples and lets you practise, so that you can use what you learn in your work."], ["end", "further", "Further learning", "If you want to learn more, ask your trainer or manager for further reading and for the next course in the series. Keep this material for reference, and tell us if anything in it is unclear or out of date so that we can improve it."]]);
more("tr.certificate", ["start", "heading", "Certificate details", "This is to certify that {{input.learner}} has completed {{input.course}}, conducted by {{input.conducted_by}}, on {{input.completed_on|date}}."]);
more("tr.attendance", ["end", "note2", "Note", "Attendance for this session is recorded by the trainer and held by HR as evidence of participation. Learners must sign only for themselves."]);
more("tr.report", [["start", "intro", "About this report", "This report on {{input.course}}, delivered by {{input.trainer}} between {{input.start_date|date}} and {{input.end_date|date}}, says how many people enrolled and completed, what the results were and what should happen next. It is prepared for the sponsor and for HR so that the value of the training can be judged and the next programme improved."], ["end", "learning", "What the results mean", "Completion is the number of learners who finished, as a share of those enrolled. Results show whether learners met the standard, and the actions above respond to what they show. The report is kept with the programme records."]]);
more("mk.profile", ["end", "values", "Our approach", "We believe in doing what we say, in treating customers and colleagues with respect, and in improving continually. This profile is kept up to date by the marketing team, and the information in it is checked before it is published."]);
more("mk.service_brochure", [["end", "process", "How we work with you", "We start by listening to your needs, then agree the scope, the timeline and the price in writing. A named person is responsible for your work, keeps you informed and is available when you have a question. When the work is done we ask for your feedback so that we can do better."], ["end", "assurance", "Our commitments", "We stand behind our work and will put right anything that does not meet what we agreed. We keep your information confidential and we follow the laws and standards that apply to our services."]]);
more("mk.product_brochure", [["start", "about", "Why this product", "{{input.product}} is designed to give you the features below with the least effort. This brochure explains what it does, what you gain and what it is made of, in language you can use to decide."], ["end", "support", "Support and warranty", "Every {{input.product}} is supported by our team, who help with installation, use and problems. Warranty terms are those stated in the sales agreement or the warranty card supplied with the product."]]);
more("mk.one_pager", ["end", "contact", "More information", "For more details, a demonstration or a quotation, please contact {{company.name}} using the details on this page. We will be pleased to answer your questions."]);
more("mk.datasheet", [["start", "intro", "Product summary", "{{input.product}}, model {{input.model}}, is described below. This datasheet gives the specifications and the typical uses so that engineers and buyers can check that it fits their requirements."], ["end", "notes", "Notes and compliance", "Specifications are those of the product as manufactured and may be changed without notice for improvement. Compliance and certification: {{input.compliance}}. For installation, safety instructions and warranty terms, see the product manual."]]);
more("mk.flyer", ["end", "note", "Good to know", "Please bring this flyer or mention it to take part. {{company.name}} reserves the right to change the details if circumstances require, and we will tell you if we do."]);
more("mk.press_release", [["end", "notes", "Notes to editors", "This announcement is issued by {{company.name}} on {{input.release_date|date}} in {{input.city}}. Statements attributed to named people are made with their consent. Interviews and images are available on request from the media contact below."], ["end", "boiler", "Media enquiries", "For more information, interviews or images, please contact {{input.media_contact}}. Please do not publish the information in this release before the date and time stated."]]);
more("mk.media_kit", [["start", "intro", "About this media kit", "This media kit gives journalists, partners and event organisers what they need to report accurately on {{company.name}}: the company description, key facts, logos and brand assets, the leadership and how to reach us. Please use the approved descriptions and assets and credit the company correctly."], ["end", "usage", "Using our name and assets", "Logos and images may be used to report on {{company.name}} and must not be altered, recoloured or used to suggest an endorsement. Please send the media contact a copy of anything you publish, so that we can check facts and share it with our team."]]);
more("mk.brand_guide", [["start", "intro", "Why brand guidelines", "These guidelines tell everyone who creates material for {{company.name}} how to use our logo, colours, type and voice, so that everything we publish looks and sounds like one company. They are owned by {{input.owner}}, and any use that differs from them needs the owner's approval."], ["end", "misuse", "Correct and incorrect use", "Do not stretch, rotate, recolour or crop the logo, place it on a busy background that makes it hard to read, or change the approved colours and typefaces. Always leave clear space around the logo. If you are unsure whether a design is correct, ask {{input.owner}} before it is published."]]);
more("mk.campaign_brief", [["start", "intro", "Purpose of this brief", "This brief for the {{input.campaign}} campaign, owned by {{input.owner}} and running from {{input.start_date|date}} to {{input.end_date|date}}, tells everyone who works on it what the campaign is for, who it is for, where it runs and what it may spend. A clear brief saves time and makes the results easier to judge."], ["end", "measure", "Measuring success and approvals", "The campaign is judged against its goals, using measures agreed before it starts and reported at the end. Creative material, claims and spend are approved by the owner before they go live, and any claim about a product or a result is checked for accuracy and for compliance with advertising rules before it is published."]]);
more("mk.content_calendar", ["end", "rules", "How to use the calendar", "Each entry has an owner and a status, and content is reviewed before it is published. Changes to dates are made in this calendar so that everyone sees them, and content that does not meet the brand guidelines or the accuracy check is not published."]);
more("lg.dpdp_notice", ["end", "grievance", "Complaints and changes to this notice", "If you are not satisfied with how we handle your personal data, you may contact {{input.officer_name}} at {{input.contact_email}}, and if your concern is not resolved you may approach the Data Protection Board of India as the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 provides. We may update this notice when our purposes or the law change, and we will tell you of material changes so that you can decide whether to continue."]);
more("lg.cookie", [["start", "purpose", "What this policy covers", "This policy explains how {{input.website}} uses cookies and similar technologies, why we use them and how you can control them. It applies from {{input.effective_date|date}}. A cookie is a small file that a website stores on your device to remember something about you or your visit."], ["end", "control", "Your choices and how to contact us", "You can accept or decline cookies that are not strictly necessary through the settings we provide on our site, and you can also change your browser settings to block or delete cookies; if you do, some parts of the site may not work as intended. We review this policy when our use of cookies changes. {{input.manage_how}} For any question, write to {{input.contact_email}}."]]);
more("lg.aup", [["start", "purpose", "Purpose and scope", "This acceptable use policy sets the rules for using {{input.service_name}}, so that it stays safe, lawful and fair for everyone. It applies to every user and to everything done through the service, from {{input.effective_date|date}}."], ["end", "enforcement", "Reporting and enforcement", "If you see use of the service that breaks this policy, please report it to {{input.report_email}}. We may investigate, remove content, suspend or end access, and report unlawful activity to the authorities, with or without notice where the law or the safety of others requires it. This policy may change, and continued use after a change means you accept the updated policy."]]);
more("lg.retention", ["end", "disposal", "Disposal, holds and review", "When the retention period for a record ends, it is securely destroyed or irreversibly anonymised, and the destruction is recorded, unless a legal hold applies. A legal hold, issued by {{input.hold_contact}}, suspends disposal of the records it names until the hold is lifted in writing. This policy is owned by {{input.owner}}, applies from {{input.effective_date|date}} and is reviewed when the law, the business or the records we hold change."]);
more("lg.affidavit", ["end", "note", "Declaration of the deponent", "I solemnly affirm and state that the contents of this affidavit are true and correct to the best of my knowledge and belief and that nothing material has been concealed. This affidavit is made for the purpose stated above and is to be executed on stamp paper of the value the law requires and, where needed, attested by a notary or other authorised officer."]);
more("lg.declaration", ["end", "closing", "Closing statement", "I declare that the information and statements above are true and complete to the best of my knowledge and belief, that I have not withheld anything that is relevant to the purpose of this declaration, and that I will tell {{company.name}} promptly if anything changes."]);

more("tr.plan", ["end", "risks", "Risks and attendance", "The main risks to the programme are low attendance, trainer availability and changes in business priorities. HR confirms attendance with managers a week before each session, arranges a replacement trainer where needed, and reports to the sponsor if the plan has to change."]);
more("tr.curriculum", ["end", "materials", "Materials and trainer requirements", "Trainers must be qualified in the subject, familiar with this curriculum and able to give feedback to learners; learners receive the materials listed for each module."]);
more("tr.lesson_plan", ["end", "equipment", "Materials and room", "The trainer prepares the materials listed against each activity, arranges the seating to suit the activities and makes sure that every learner can see and hear. Time is kept so that the closing activity is not rushed."]);
more("tr.material", ["end", "use", "How to use this material", "Work through the sections in order. Stop at the exercises and try them yourself before reading on. If you are using this material in a course, bring your questions to the next session."]);
more("tr.certificate", ["end", "validity", "Validity", "This certificate records completion of the course named above and does not by itself confer any professional qualification."]);
more("tr.report", ["end", "followup", "Feedback and costs", "Participants' feedback was collected after the sessions and is summarised in the results above. HR holds the detailed feedback, the attendance records and the costs, which are available to the sponsor on request."]);
more("mk.service_brochure", ["end", "faq", "Questions we are often asked", "Customers often ask how long the work takes, how it is priced and what happens if their needs change. The answers depend on your requirement; we give them in writing before you decide, and we are happy to talk them through."]);
more("mk.media_kit", ["end", "usage2", "Interviews and images", "We can arrange interviews with our leadership and supply high-resolution images and approved quotes on request, so that your story is accurate and complete."]);
more("mk.brand_guide", ["end", "assets", "Where to find assets", "Approved logo files, colour values and fonts are kept by {{input.owner}} and shared on request. Always use the original files and never recreate the logo from a screenshot."]);
more("lg.cookie", ["end", "types", "Types of cookie", "Strictly necessary cookies make the site work and cannot be switched off. Preference cookies remember your choices. Analytics cookies help us understand how the site is used, and are set only with your consent. Advertising cookies, if any, are listed in the table above and are also set only with your consent."]);
more("lg.aup", ["end", "rules2", "Your responsibilities", "You are responsible for your account and for everything done through it, for keeping your credentials secret, and for making sure that anything you upload or send is lawful and that you have the right to share it. You must not interfere with the service, try to reach what you are not authorised to use, or use it to harm others."]);

more("tr.report", ["end", "recommend", "Recommendations", "Based on the results, the trainer and HR recommend whether the programme should be repeated as it is, changed, or stopped, and which learners should receive further support. The sponsor decides, and the decision is recorded."]);
more("mk.service_brochure", ["end", "contact3", "Getting started", "To get started, tell us about your need and we will respond within a working day."]);
more("mk.media_kit", ["end", "embargo", "Embargoes and approvals", "Unless a document is marked as embargoed it may be used immediately; embargoed material must not be published before the time stated. Direct quotes from our people must be approved by the media contact before publication."]);
more("lg.cookie", ["end", "retention2", "How long cookies last", "Session cookies are deleted when you close your browser; persistent cookies remain for the duration stated in the table above, unless you delete them sooner."]);
